PR title: Add basic test for MDLL

Source: https://github.com/StanfordVLSI/dragonphy2/pull/94

PR description:
The PR resolves issue #93 by implementing a basic test for the MDLL (Multiplying Delay-Locked Loop). According to the author, an external clock is fed into the reference clock pins, and various signals are controlled to route the MDLL output clock through the analog and digital cores.

The submission includes "a record of the steps that have to be taken to use the MDLL," which the author notes may be useful for laboratory testing. Key configuration steps documented include:

- Enabling the reference clock buffer
- Taking the MDLL out of reset and enabling the oscillator
- Selecting the MDLL clock as the analog core source
- Bypassing the initial divide-by-two stage

